040, 1098, 1283). The\r\n  guardrail (MAX_SUMMARY_CHARS in codec.rs) was raised 600 �� 20,000 by commit f9842276 at 2026-08-15 10:00 EDT. That commit is an ancestor of the source HEAD the current\r\n  binary was built from, and the 18:30 EDT daemon restart put that fixed binary live (verified: the running process's /proc/exe is the exact current on-disk binary, same\r\n  inode, not a replaced-after-start image). No action needed here �X these were failures of the prior daemon instance and won't recur. They matter only because every goal\r\n  they killed then fell into defect #1 on its next round.\r\n\r\n  3. Agent command-channel lost mid-run (provider failure) �X prior daemon instance.\r\n  failed to read Goal Agent command channel /insurity/refine/run/8082/processes/goal-agent-<uuid>.commands.jsonl: No such file or directory (os error 2) �X the agent IPC file\r\n  disappeared during the run. Hit 3 goals, clustered 16:30�V16:41 UTC (before the 18:30 EDT restart). The daemon currently reports degraded_integrations:\r\n  [\"operation-recovery-interrupted\"], which corroborates instability around agent process lifecycle. Worth investigating whether it recurs on the current daemon.\r\n\r\n  4. Fleet node-ownership mismatch on Quality (PHI goal).\r\n  Quality failed: Goal 00000SZ65PBBNHVG7B24N80001 is owned by node bo2lnxnevo03-buddy, not active node BO2LNXIPSAPP01 �X a goal owned by one node was picked up for Quality by\r\n  a different node. Ownership/routing bug, not code.\r\n\r\n  5. Integration/reconciliation churn on the two oldest goals (Batch Reserve & PHI).\r\n  Both produced completed, Governance-passing candidates that then failed to land: stale_candidate (target base moved), then a merge CONFLICT in\r\n  batch-reserve-approval.component.ts because a sibling goal had already landed the same fix, then already_merged_reconciliation_unsafe / \"lacks durable passed isolated\r\n  Quality evidence.\" This is the known consequence of multiple parallel goals integrating into one shared insurity-claims checkout �X the fixes are essentially done; the\r\n  platform can't reconcile them.\r\n\r\n  Impact: two of these are high-value �X Batch Reserve Reject (Financials) and HIPAA PHI-role gating (CXP-16640). For both, the implementation was completed and passed\r\n  Governance; they're blocked purely on Refine plumbing (revise-stage JSON for Batch Reserve, node ownership + reconciliation for PHI).\r\n\r\n  Recommended actions\r\n  1. Fix defect #1 (revise-stage structured-plan decode / criticism_id handling in codec.rs / the revise prompt) �X it is the active wall and reproduces on the current\r\n  daemon; no amount of re-queuing gets past it.\r\n  2. Investigate the operation-recovery-interrupted degraded integration and the command-channel-file loss (defect #3); confirm whether it still occurs post-restart.\r\n  3. Fix the fleet node-ownership routing (defect #4) so Quality runs on the owning node.\r\n  4. For Batch Reserve and PHI, recover the already-Governance-passed candidates rather than re-planning from scratch; the code exists.\r\n\r\n  I can pull the exact candidate commit hashes and per-round evidence for any of these on request.\r\n\r\n\r\n[cid:insurity-small2_2f81c33c-d951-4e5c-a467-1113541ca22c.jpg]\r\nBuddy Williams\r\nBuddy.Williams@insurity.com\r\n\r\n[cid:excellence2026signature(17b0688e-5473-4b74-96eb-a73f633f2c2f)_48407359-d77b-4967-95cd-277a32b50ebc.png]<https://insurity.com/excellence?utm_source=Email-Signature&utm_medium=Email&utm_campaign=Event-Excellence-2026>\r\n\r\n_____________________________________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThe information contained in this e-mail message is intended only for the personal and confidential use of the intended recipient(s). This message may be an attorney-client communication and/or work product and as such is privileged and confidential. If the reader of this message is not the intended recipient or an agent responsible for de